From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blackhat-7 <44942105+blackhat-7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 05:29:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 08/33] CPU expert pool: UMWAIT parking on Linux
 (STRATA_UMWAIT) and guided task sizes (STRATA_POOL_GUIDED), gfx1100 defaults

Port of opt7/integrate 561d53da 6e2da6eb 60606238 e5f187ee onto v0.2.9's pool (NUMA slices, native families):
- STRATA_UMWAIT=1 (Linux, WAITPKG CPUs; gfx1100 table): a parked worker and the verifier's doorbell wait poll with
  UMWAIT in C0.2 on the line the host / GPU writes (umwait.hpp), instead of a pause spin. v0.2.9's own
  STRATA_POOL_UMWAIT is built for MSVC only and stays as it is.
- STRATA_POOL_GUIDED=C (gfx1100 table: 32): an unsliced multi phase's automatic tasks shrink as it runs out
  (plan_phase -> bounds_), so a slow core's last task does not hold the phase; NUMA-sliced phases keep v0.2.9's
  equal cut. Rows are computed the same way whoever takes them.
- STRATA_POOL_PROF=1: per-thread phase profile (measurement).
Measured on 0.1.43: same decode speed with ~20 W less and max 82 C (was 86); guided: pool -8% a round, edit +2.8%.
